```go
if len(commitHash) == 12 {
```

You could use:
```go
import "entire.io/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/id"

// ...
if cpID, err := id.NewCheckpointID(commitHash); err == nil {
    // valid checkpoint ID
}
```

Or just use `id.Validate(commitHash) == nil` if you don't need the typed value.

This would be more robust since it validates the format (12 lowercase hex chars) rather than just length.

